-- [Physical Starters] Nose Figure Eight
UPDATE activities
SET activity = 'Nose Figure Eight',
    time = 3,
    description = '<p>Start the session with Nose Figure Eight to wake the body. Imagine you have a pencil on the end of your nose and a sheet of paper in front of you.</p><p><strong>Why it works</strong></p><ul><li>Releases tension before singing</li><li>Aligns posture for freer breath and tone</li><li>Gets the whole class moving as one ensemble</li></ul>',
    activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space with room to stretch and turn. Whole class. No props needed. About 3 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to do it</strong></p><ol><li>Imagine you have a pencil on the end of your nose and a sheet of paper in front of you.</li><li>Slowly draw a lazy figure of 8 (on its side) with your imaginary pencil.</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>During Nose Figure Eight, use one short posture cue only (‘soft knees’ or ‘long spine’) so movement stays musical.</li><li>After Nose Figure Eight, shake out once, then find ‘singer’s feet’ before the first note.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Do the movement without chant/song first, then add the voice.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Add an opposite pattern or faster swap on a shared cue.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Freeze in the final aligned posture and take one supported breath together.</p>',
