    activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Stand or sit tall with free shoulders. Whole class. No props needed. About 2 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to do it</strong></p><ol><li>Gather focus and watch the teacher model once in silence.</li><li>‘Hot Potato’ warm-up from ‘SingUp’.</li><li>Repeat together, then try once more with greater clarity.</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>In Hot Potato, pause after the first full cycle and ask one pupil what they felt move — name that sensation.</li><li>Repeat Hot Potato once seated if standing posture collapsed — compare the two sensations.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Teacher models one slow cycle; class joins on the out-breath only.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Siren through a wider interval, then land softly on a sung ‘ah’.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Transfer the same breath feeling into the opening line of today’s repertoire.</p>',
