    description = '<p>Warm the face and diction with Bogapilla. Say the word ‘Bogapilla’ in as many different ways as possible for the choir to copy.</p><p><strong>Why it works</strong></p><ul><li>Wakes facial muscles for clear diction</li><li>Improves articulation without forcing the voice</li><li>Makes warm-up playful so diction feels low-stakes</li></ul>',
    activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Standing or seated circle so everyone can see mouths. No props needed. About 2 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to do it</strong></p><ol><li>Gather focus and watch the teacher model once in silence.</li><li>Say the word ‘Bogapilla’ in as many different ways as possible for the choir to copy.</li><li>Repeat together, then try once more with greater clarity.</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>For Bogapilla, contrast a muddy version with a crystal-clear version so the diction target is obvious.</li><li>After Bogapilla, spot one consonant that still smudges and drill only that word.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Speak the pattern slowly in unison before any pitch or speed challenge.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Raise the tempo or move the pattern up by semitones while keeping every consonant.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Drop the warm-up consonants into a tricky lyric from the song.</p>',
