    description = '<p>Explore pitch and listening with Top-Down Canon Pattern. Then repeat starting at the top with 8 878 87678 8765678 etc.</p><p><strong>Why it works</strong></p><ul><li>Explores pitch range safely and playfully</li><li>Builds listening and pitch-matching accuracy</li><li>Smooths register transitions without pushing</li></ul>',
    activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Standing circle or open rows facing the leader. Optional: piano or pitch reference. About 3 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to do it</strong></p><ol><li>Then repeat starting at the top with 8 878 87678 8765678 etc.</li><li>Split the group in two and repeat in canon, with the 2nd group coming in on beat 3 of bar 1, or sing ‘1 121’ and ‘8 878’ simultaneously.</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>On Top-Down Canon Pattern, isolate the hardest pitch gesture once, then rejoin the full pattern at a slower tempo.</li><li>After Top-Down Canon Pattern, sing the first phrase of the song on ‘ng’ using the same freedom.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Narrow the pitch range and let the class echo the leader phrase by phrase.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Siren through a wider interval, then land softly on a sung ‘ah’.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Improvise a four-beat answer after the set pattern, still matching the leader’s vowel.</p>',
