-- Drama tip refresh: Emotion Statues
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. Props: hat and emotion slips. About 10 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Teacher calls out emotions (happy, scared, angry, excited)</li><li>Children freeze in full-body ''statue'' showing that feeling</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Use one sharp freeze cue for Emotion Statues; hold three silent counts before you speak so stillness sticks.</li><li>Name the emotion once, then coach body not face — ‘show it in your spine/hands’ keeps it performable.</li><li>If Emotion Statues frays, shrink the group size for one round, then rebuild to whole class.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Teacher models first; children copy as a whole group before trying in pairs.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Add a second cue (speed, size or emotion) once the basic game is secure.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Link to a story book face or feeling word of the day.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '1be62bd5-87b0-46d8-b963-38c825d509ea';

-- Drama tip refresh: Invisible Ball Pass
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear space so the class can sit or stand in a circle. No props needed. About 10 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Stand in circle pretending to pass balls of different sizes, weights and textures</li><li>Name the object (''heavy watermelon'', ''hot potato'') and respond physically</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Demand clear weight and size: if the audience can’t ‘see’ it, freeze and remime the first handle.</li><li>Keep the circle tight enough to hear; if the pass breaks, rewind two people and restart the chain.</li><li>Name one precise success after Invisible Ball Pass (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Teacher models first; children copy as a whole group before trying in pairs.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Demand clearer weight, size and texture so the audience can ''see'' the object.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = 'a38af99a-42f9-47ec-ba8c-acaf011b652b';

