SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. Whole class. No props needed. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Gather attention and explain the game in one short sentence.</li><li>A ''conductor'' stands in front of the group and points to different sections, who must create the sound and action of a specific instrument (e.g., ''violins'' hum a high note, ''drums'' stomp feet).</li><li>Play a second round with a fresh prompt, then share one strong moment with the class.</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Layer one sound at a time; conductor cuts with a flat hand so the texture doesn’t turn to noise.</li><li>After The Human Orchestra, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in The Human Orchestra and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Reduce choices and model the first round together.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Layer dynamics (loud/soft, near/far) and keep a shared pulse.</p>',
