-- Drama tip refresh: The Conductor
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. Whole class. No props needed. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>A ''conductor'' stands in front of the group</li><li>The group produces a single, continuous sound</li><li>The conductor uses hand gestures to make the sound louder, softer, faster, slower, and cut out sections</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Before The Conductor, model the first ten seconds yourself so the rule is visible, not only explained.</li><li>After The Conductor, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in The Conductor and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Reduce choices and model the first round together.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Layer dynamics (loud/soft, near/far) and keep a shared pulse.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = 'b3bc87ec-1f1f-4057-b336-3c9154d0a4bd';

-- Drama tip refresh: Giant and Dwarf
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. No props needed. About 10 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Pupils walk normally</li><li>On cue, they change to a very slow, giant-like walk or a very fast, tiny-dwarf-like scurry</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Before Giant and Dwarf, model the first ten seconds yourself so the rule is visible, not only explained.</li><li>After Giant and Dwarf, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>If Giant and Dwarf frays, shrink the group size for one round, then rebuild to whole class.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Reduce choices and model the first round together.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Add a time limit, a second rule, or ask pairs to share one polished moment.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = 'fa14224f-79b5-43ce-b54b-e8e338626efc';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Magical Garden
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. No props needed. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Pupils pretend to be different plants or creatures in a magical garden</li><li>The teacher describes what is happening in the garden (e.g</li><li>''the sun is out'', ''a storm is coming''). Pupils react with movement</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Before The Magical Garden, model the first ten seconds yourself so the rule is visible, not only explained.</li><li>After The Magical Garden, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in The Magical Garden and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Reduce choices and model the first round together.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Add a time limit, a second rule, or ask pairs to share one polished moment.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '26774287-ab2a-4eec-be68-9a4d2ad24e72';

-- Drama tip refresh: Pass the Sound
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear space so the class can sit or stand in a circle. No props needed. About 10 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Pupils sit in a circle</li><li>One person creates a simple sound and an accompanying gesture</li><li>The next person copies it exactly and passes it on, like ''telephone''</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Keep the circle tight enough to hear; if the pass breaks, rewind two people and restart the chain.</li><li>After Pass the Sound, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>If Pass the Sound frays, shrink the group size for one round, then rebuild to whole class.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Reduce choices and model the first round together.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Layer dynamics (loud/soft, near/far) and keep a shared pulse.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '05bd2d13-937d-4a74-bcaa-70d6f199d356';

-- Drama tip refresh: Role Play Scenarios
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space. Work in small groups. No props needed. About 20 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>The teacher presents simple scenarios (e.g</li><li>''two friends meet at the park'', ''a trip to the zoo'')</li><li>Small groups of pupils improvise a short scene based on the prompt</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>For Role Play Scenarios, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>After Role Play Scenarios, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Name one precise success after Role Play Scenarios (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Reduce choices and model the first round together.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '8008a163-3b8a-46f6-8501-3a45877566ea';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Weather Report
