-- Drama tip refresh: Silent Movie
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. Props: optional music player. About 20 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Gather attention and explain the game in one short sentence.</li><li>The class acts out a short, well-known fairy tale or story with no dialogue, only music and exaggerated mime.</li><li>Play a second round with a fresh prompt, then share one strong moment with the class.</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Demand clear weight and size: if the audience can’t ‘see’ it, freeze and remime the first handle.</li><li>For Silent Movie, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>Keep tracks short and fade early so freezes land on silence, not a long outro.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Reduce choices and model the first round together.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '500306af-14cd-458b-bf3e-b7dc06c3fc79';

-- Drama tip refresh: Freeze and Guess
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space with clear pathways. No props needed. About 10 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Pupils move around the room</li><li>The teacher shouts ''Freeze!'' and pupils must hold a pose</li><li>The teacher then prompts them with ''What could you be?''</li><li>Pupils can then whisper their idea</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Use one sharp freeze cue for Freeze and Guess; hold three silent counts before you speak so stillness sticks.</li><li>After Freeze and Guess, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>If Freeze and Guess frays, shrink the group size for one round, then rebuild to whole class.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Reduce choices and model the first round together.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Add a time limit, a second rule, or ask pairs to share one polished moment.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '1a66d90c-fa8d-441f-8070-7e52cbcef3b4';

-- Drama tip refresh: Three-Line Scenes
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space. Children work in pairs. No props needed. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>In pairs, pupils are given a setting and two characters</li><li>They must improvise a scene that lasts for only three lines of dialogue</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>For Three-Line Scenes, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>In Three-Line Scenes, swap leaders halfway so both partners make offers, not just the confident one.</li><li>Name one precise success after Three-Line Scenes (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Work as a whole class first, then try with a partner.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = 'bc2b86cb-3f58-455e-bbf9-c003b76ec712';

