-- Drama tip refresh: The Human Statue Museum
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. Props: optional light switch or ''lights'' cue. About 10 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Pupils pretend to be statues in a museum</li><li>The teacher is the ''curator'' who turns the lights on and off</li><li>When the lights are on, the statues must be perfectly still</li><li>When they are off, they can move and change their pose</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Use one sharp freeze cue for The Human Statue Museum; hold three silent counts before you speak so stillness sticks.</li><li>After The Human Statue Museum, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>If The Human Statue Museum frays, shrink the group size for one round, then rebuild to whole class.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Reduce choices and model the first round together.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Add a time limit, a second rule, or ask pairs to share one polished moment.</p>',
