-- Drama tip refresh: The Living Room
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space with clear pathways. No props needed. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Pupils stand in a circle and pretend to be different pieces of furniture in a living room</li><li>The teacher or another student can then enter the ''room'' and interact with the ''furniture''</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Before The Living Room, model the first ten seconds yourself so the rule is visible, not only explained.</li><li>After The Living Room, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in The Living Room and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Reduce choices and model the first round together.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Add a time limit, a second rule, or ask pairs to share one polished moment.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '4cb7321d-fe27-4653-a996-3b8caa16b0a9';

-- Drama tip refresh: Yes, and...
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space. Children work in pairs. No props needed. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>In pairs, pupils improvise a scene</li><li>One person starts with a sentence</li><li>The other person must respond with a sentence that starts with ''Yes, and...'' and adds new information to the scene</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Side-coach only with ‘accept and add’ — block any ‘no’ / ‘but’ and replay the last offer.</li><li>For Yes, and..., allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>Name one precise success after Yes, and... (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Work as a whole class first, then try with a partner.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Replay the strongest 20 seconds and polish one offer.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '431bf974-e769-4a77-b8e2-6b2a7b356e2d';

-- Drama tip refresh: Character in the Hot Seat
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. Props: chairs. About 20 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>One student is selected to sit in the ''hot seat''</li><li>They are given a character role (e.g. an astronaut, a grumpy shopkeeper) and must answer questions from the class in character</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Protect the hot-seat player: questions stay kind, in-role, and you may veto anything personal.</li><li>After Character in the Hot Seat, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Name one precise success after Character in the Hot Seat (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Raise the challenge with constraints (no words, fixed emotion, or a tighter time limit).</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Write a diary entry or thought-track in role afterwards.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '0a9640ec-2790-467e-9754-8f73b82d60a1';

-- Drama tip refresh: Soundscape Story
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. No props needed. About 20 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>The class works together to create a full soundscape for a story</li><li>Pupils are assigned different sounds (e.g., wind, car horns, footsteps) and must create them on cue from a ''director''</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Layer one sound at a time; conductor cuts with a flat hand so the texture doesn’t turn to noise.</li><li>After Soundscape Story, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>If Soundscape Story frays, shrink the group size for one round, then rebuild to whole class.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Layer dynamics (loud/soft, near/far) and keep a shared pulse.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Perform the soundscape under a short narrated story.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '551f55b1-74a7-4c6b-81b0-f2c86fca11c1';

-- Drama tip refresh: Emotion Mask
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. Props: hat and emotion slips. About 10 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Pupils create an ''emotion mask'' with their hands over their face</li><li>They then make a facial expression</li><li>When they lower their hands, they must hold that expression perfectly still for the class to guess</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Name the emotion once, then coach body not face — ‘show it in your spine/hands’ keeps it performable.</li><li>After Emotion Mask, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Name one precise success after Emotion Mask (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Raise the challenge with constraints (no words, fixed emotion, or a tighter time limit).</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '47ff2677-5390-453e-9586-37bcd9296920';

-- Drama tip refresh: Three-Scene Plays
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space. Work in small groups. No props needed. About 30 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Organise the class into small groups and give them a clear playing space.</li><li>In small groups, pupils are given a simple plot (e.g. a mystery, a rescue) and must create a short play with a clear beginning, middle, and end, using three distinct scenes.</li><li>Play a second round with a fresh prompt, then share one strong moment with the class.</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>For Three-Scene Plays, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>After Three-Scene Plays, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in Three-Scene Plays and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Replay the strongest 20 seconds and polish one offer.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '046afaa6-7034-4c3e-b2f6-8a8334f455ff';

-- Drama tip refresh: Gibberish Translator
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space. Children work in pairs. Props: hat and emotion slips. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>In pairs, one person speaks in a made-up language (gibberish) with a clear emotion or intention</li><li>The other person ''translates'' what they are saying, creating an improvised scene</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Name the emotion once, then coach body not face — ‘show it in your spine/hands’ keeps it performable.</li><li>For Gibberish Translator, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>Push emotion and intention in the gibberish; translator must answer the feeling, not invent a random plot.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Work as a whole class first, then try with a partner.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Replay the strongest 20 seconds and polish one offer.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '7b8588eb-e632-4e75-abcc-bf7b6349a457';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Living Tableau
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space. Work in small groups. Whole class. No props needed. About 20 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>A group of pupils creates a frozen picture (tableau) of a specific scene (e.g</li><li>''a moment from history'', ''a crowded city street'')</li><li>On a cue, one person in the tableau says their inner thoughts</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Use one sharp freeze cue for The Living Tableau; hold three silent counts before you speak so stillness sticks.</li><li>For The Living Tableau, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>Name one precise success after The Living Tableau (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Bring one statue to life for five seconds, then freeze again.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '9dc9d904-e61e-4807-9dcd-550f9555d0ea';

-- Drama tip refresh: Character Walks
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space with clear pathways. No props needed. About 10 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>The teacher calls out a character type (e.g., ''a sneaky spy'', ''a proud queen'')</li><li>Pupils must walk around the space embodying that character</li><li>The teacher can give more complex prompts (e.g., ''a sneaky spy walking on a creaky floor'')</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Before Character Walks, model the first ten seconds yourself so the rule is visible, not only explained.</li><li>After Character Walks, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in Character Walks and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Raise the challenge with constraints (no words, fixed emotion, or a tighter time limit).</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '6fcfeeb6-dfbb-4b8e-bf1e-f78c79953cba';

-- Drama tip refresh: Conscience Alley
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. No props needed. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>One student stands at one end of two lines of pupils facing each other</li><li>As they walk down the ''alley'', pupils on each side whisper advice or thoughts from a character''s ''conscience''</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Voices in the alley stay at advice volume — no shouting in the walker’s ears; swap the walker often.</li><li>After Conscience Alley, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>If Conscience Alley frays, shrink the group size for one round, then rebuild to whole class.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Raise the challenge with constraints (no words, fixed emotion, or a tighter time limit).</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '19fdd9ef-4d2c-4445-bd75-c260c7be0d76';

-- Drama tip refresh: Director's Cut
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. No props needed. About 20 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Two or three pupils improvise a scene</li><li>The rest of the class are ''directors'' who can shout ''Cut!'' and give a direction for the actors to follow (e.g., ''Do that faster!'', ''Show us how you feel!'')</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>For Director''s Cut, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>After Director''s Cut, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in Director''s Cut and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Replay the strongest 20 seconds and polish one offer.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '69efa24e-c15f-4566-8f69-c2f0518359f4';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Human Machine
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. No props needed. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Each student adds a simple, repetitive movement and sound to create an increasingly complex ''machine''</li><li>The ''director'' can then control the machine by speeding it up or slowing it down</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Each new part must connect physically to the last; pause to tighten rhythm before adding more pupils.</li><li>After The Human Machine, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in The Human Machine and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Layer dynamics (loud/soft, near/far) and keep a shared pulse.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
