-- Drama tip refresh: Found Object Story
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space. Work in small groups. Props: one everyday object. About 25 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Pupils are given a random, everyday object (e.g. a shoe, a bottle, a piece of string)</li><li>In small groups, they must create a short play where the object is the central character or prop</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Before Found Object Story, model the first ten seconds yourself so the rule is visible, not only explained.</li><li>After Found Object Story, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in Found Object Story and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p>',
