-- Drama tip refresh: Back-to-Back Scenes
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space. Children work in pairs. No props needed. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>In pairs, pupils sit back-to-back</li><li>The teacher gives them a scene scenario</li><li>They must improvise the scene using only their voices, focusing on dialogue, tone, and vocal nuance</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>For Back-to-Back Scenes, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>In Back-to-Back Scenes, swap leaders halfway so both partners make offers, not just the confident one.</li><li>Name one precise success after Back-to-Back Scenes (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Work as a whole class first, then try with a partner.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Replay the strongest 20 seconds and polish one offer.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
