-- Drama tip refresh: One-Minute Scenes
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space. Children work in pairs. No props needed. About 20 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>In pairs, pupils are given a simple prompt (e.g</li><li>''meeting a stranger'', ''losing something important'') and must create a scene that lasts for exactly one minute</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>For One-Minute Scenes, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>In One-Minute Scenes, swap leaders halfway so both partners make offers, not just the confident one.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in One-Minute Scenes and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Work as a whole class first, then try with a partner.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Replay the strongest 20 seconds and polish one offer.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '2ddb39f8-5a21-4917-87c3-b05bc2fb0868';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Human Photograph
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. No props needed. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>The teacher calls out a setting or situation (e.g</li><li>''a family dinner'', ''the playground at lunchtime'')</li><li>The class works together to quickly form a frozen tableau that tells a story about that moment</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Use one sharp freeze cue for The Human Photograph; hold three silent counts before you speak so stillness sticks.</li><li>After The Human Photograph, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>If The Human Photograph frays, shrink the group size for one round, then rebuild to whole class.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Bring one statue to life for five seconds, then freeze again.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '5492daab-50cb-4140-833d-25ead36cd4fe';

-- Drama tip refresh: Story Cards
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space. Work in small groups. Props: character, setting and problem cards. About 25 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Pupils are given a set of cards with a character, a setting, and a problem</li><li>In small groups, they must create and perform a short play that incorporates all three elements</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Before Story Cards, model the first ten seconds yourself so the rule is visible, not only explained.</li><li>After Story Cards, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>If Story Cards frays, shrink the group size for one round, then rebuild to whole class.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '39f73103-2511-42bd-ab52-df593d283a92';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Emotion Tunnel
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. Props: hat and emotion slips. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Pupils form two lines facing each other</li><li>One student walks down the middle, and the pupils on each side whisper different emotions or feelings that the person walking should embody</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Name the emotion once, then coach body not face — ‘show it in your spine/hands’ keeps it performable.</li><li>Voices in the alley stay at advice volume — no shouting in the walker’s ears; swap the walker often.</li><li>Name one precise success after The Emotion Tunnel (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Raise the challenge with constraints (no words, fixed emotion, or a tighter time limit).</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '5bb1a5b6-4f52-4250-9e20-f505525f1815';

-- Drama tip refresh: What's in the Box?
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. No props needed. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>A student mimes opening a box and reacting to the invisible object inside</li><li>Another student then enters and reacts to the same invisible object</li><li>The scene continues with others joining in</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Demand clear weight and size: if the audience can’t ‘see’ it, freeze and remime the first handle.</li><li>For What''s in the Box?, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>If What''s in the Box? frays, shrink the group size for one round, then rebuild to whole class.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Replay the strongest 20 seconds and polish one offer.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = 'bbfb4851-8f67-40a2-8edb-56cfaa8e947c';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Invisible Rope
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear space so the class can sit or stand in a circle. No props needed. About 10 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>In a circle, pupils hold an imaginary rope</li><li>The ''leader'' can change the rope''s texture, weight, or temperature, and the other pupils must react in unison</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Demand clear weight and size: if the audience can’t ‘see’ it, freeze and remime the first handle.</li><li>After The Invisible Rope, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in The Invisible Rope and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Demand clearer weight, size and texture so the audience can ''see'' the object.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '4c725e22-a15a-4bf5-8e07-b3c2d567b5fd';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Monologue
