-- Drama tip refresh: Vocal Stretches
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. No props needed. About 5 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Gather attention and explain the game in one short sentence.</li><li>Pupils practice vocal warm-up exercises like buzzing, humming, and mouth stretches to prepare their voices for performance.</li><li>Play a second round with a fresh prompt, then share one strong moment with the class.</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Before Vocal Stretches, model the first ten seconds yourself so the rule is visible, not only explained.</li><li>After Vocal Stretches, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in Vocal Stretches and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Raise the challenge with constraints (no words, fixed emotion, or a tighter time limit).</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = 'e9a9414c-e664-4586-8f25-abac95a0173c';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Three-Part Story
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space. Work in small groups. No props needed. About 25 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>The teacher gives a beginning, middle, and end to a story</li><li>Pupils work in groups to create a short play that fits this structure, filling in the details with their own ideas</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Before The Three-Part Story, model the first ten seconds yourself so the rule is visible, not only explained.</li><li>After The Three-Part Story, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in The Three-Part Story and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = 'ce53ad45-edec-4e0d-83c0-f23558119a45';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Human Car
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space with clear pathways. No props needed. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Gather attention and explain the game in one short sentence.</li><li>Pupils form a ''car'' with their bodies and must move around the room as one unit, making engine sounds and reacting to imaginary ''traffic''.</li><li>Play a second round with a fresh prompt, then share one strong moment with the class.</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Demand clear weight and size: if the audience can’t ‘see’ it, freeze and remime the first handle.</li><li>After The Human Car, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>If The Human Car frays, shrink the group size for one round, then rebuild to whole class.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Layer dynamics (loud/soft, near/far) and keep a shared pulse.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = 'fe194e2a-050e-4a92-bb81-1c17bcdf0286';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Emotion Swap
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space. Children work in pairs. Props: hat and emotion slips. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>In pairs, pupils improvise a simple scene</li><li>The teacher calls out an emotion, and both pupils must immediately switch to that emotion, changing the tone and direction of the scene</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Name the emotion once, then coach body not face — ‘show it in your spine/hands’ keeps it performable.</li><li>For The Emotion Swap, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>Name one precise success after The Emotion Swap (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Work as a whole class first, then try with a partner.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Replay the strongest 20 seconds and polish one offer.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '7e4e8de9-579d-4ff4-b459-b3ed2e3f63d1';

-- Drama tip refresh: Table Read
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear space so the class can sit or stand in a circle. Props: short scripts or student-written scenes. About 20 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Pupils are given a short script (or a script they have written themselves)</li><li>They sit in a circle and read the script aloud, focusing on vocal performance, tone, and character</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Before Table Read, model the first ten seconds yourself so the rule is visible, not only explained.</li><li>After Table Read, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Scan the edges of the room in Table Read and bring a quieter pupil in to lead the next micro-round.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Raise the challenge with constraints (no words, fixed emotion, or a tighter time limit).</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = 'b6a2cc63-20a4-4074-9000-ccf3e34c21e9';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Prop Box
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. Props: a few simple props (scarf, hat, cup). About 20 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>A box is filled with a variety of unusual props</li><li>Pupils take turns reaching in and pulling one out</li><li>They must then create a short, one-minute scene that features the prop in a creative and unexpected way</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>For The Prop Box, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>After The Prop Box, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>If The Prop Box frays, shrink the group size for one round, then rebuild to whole class.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Replay the strongest 20 seconds and polish one offer.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '90706ca0-435e-4c1c-8ff4-75988935c8d6';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Silent Walk
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space with clear pathways. No props needed. About 10 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>The class walks around the room silently</li><li>The teacher claps once to stop, twice to turn and face a partner, and three times to sit down</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Before The Silent Walk, model the first ten seconds yourself so the rule is visible, not only explained.</li><li>In The Silent Walk, swap leaders halfway so both partners make offers, not just the confident one.</li><li>Name one precise success after The Silent Walk (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Raise the challenge with constraints (no words, fixed emotion, or a tighter time limit).</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '39f1c958-c3d2-4525-9f23-9a818ea1dc3f';

-- Drama tip refresh: Emotion Machine
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear floor space for movement. Props: hat and emotion slips. About 15 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Pupils work together to create a machine that makes or changes emotions</li><li>Each student adds a sound and movement to the machine</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Name the emotion once, then coach body not face — ‘show it in your spine/hands’ keeps it performable.</li><li>Each new part must connect physically to the last; pause to tighten rhythm before adding more pupils.</li><li>Name one precise success after Emotion Machine (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Layer dynamics (loud/soft, near/far) and keep a shared pulse.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '1af23154-e261-4f83-82f5-5f72390903ef';

-- Drama tip refresh: Character Profile Walk
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space with clear pathways. No props needed. About 20 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Pupils are given a character profile and walk around the room as that character</li><li>When they bump into another character, they improvise a short, two-line conversation</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>For Character Profile Walk, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>After Character Profile Walk, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>If Character Profile Walk frays, shrink the group size for one round, then rebuild to whole class.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Raise the challenge with constraints (no words, fixed emotion, or a tighter time limit).</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Replay the strongest 20 seconds and polish one offer.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '9db6d0f9-997b-4476-b809-2f1e3c0d9963';

-- Drama tip refresh: The Story of an Object
