SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Open floor space with clear pathways. Props: a brought-in object (optional). About 25 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>A student brings in an object from home</li><li>The class then works together to create a short, improvised play that tells the story of that object, from its creation to its journey to the classroom</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>For The Story of an Object, allow one planning whisper only; then commit — stop the scene solely for safety or a clear reset.</li><li>After The Story of an Object, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Name one precise success after The Story of an Object (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Require a clear beginning, middle and end within the time limit.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Replay the strongest 20 seconds and polish one offer.</p>',
