-- Drama tip refresh: Goodbye Circle
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Clear space so the class can sit or stand in a circle. No props needed. About 5 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>The class stands in a circle</li><li>The teacher or a student leads a fun, physical goodbye ritual, such as a group bow, a final cheer, or a wave that gets bigger and bigger</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Before Goodbye Circle, model the first ten seconds yourself so the rule is visible, not only explained.</li><li>After Goodbye Circle, ask for one concrete example of good listening or a bold offer before you reset.</li><li>Name one precise success after Goodbye Circle (‘clear freeze’, ‘brave offer’) before you reset.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Give a clearer prompt or allow a short planning whisper before performing.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Raise the challenge with constraints (no words, fixed emotion, or a tighter time limit).</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = '62f7031a-a529-458e-a374-b51ef84968cc';

-- Drama tip refresh: Bubble Gum Warm Up
UPDATE activities
SET activity_text = '<p><strong>Setup</strong></p><p>Sit or stand in a circle with clear floor space. No props needed — the gum is imaginary. About 10 minutes.</p><p><strong>How to play</strong></p><ol><li>Mime taking a piece of chewing gum from your pocket and putting it in your mouth (invent a silly flavour together).</li><li>Chew with big, clear exaggeration so everyone can see.</li><li>Stick the imaginary gum onto the person next to you in a new place each time (nose, shoe, hair, elbow).</li><li>Pass the gum around the circle, each child finding a different way to stick and peel it off.</li><li>Optional finish: stretch the gum between two children, then ''snap'' it and freeze.</li></ol><p><strong>Teacher tips</strong></p><ul><li>Use one sharp freeze cue for Bubble Gum Warm Up; hold three silent counts before you speak so stillness sticks.</li><li>Demand clear weight and size: if the audience can’t ‘see’ it, freeze and remime the first handle.</li><li>Keep the circle tight enough to hear; if the pass breaks, rewind two people and restart the chain.</li></ul><p><strong>Make it easier</strong></p><p>Teacher leads the first full circuit while children copy the chew together.</p><p><strong>Make it harder</strong></p><p>Add a rule: no repeating a stick-spot that has already been used.</p><p><strong>Extension</strong></p><p>Invent a tiny story about where the gum came from before you pass it on.</p>',
    updated_at = NOW()
WHERE id = 'bc7a8c5e-d06e-43fe-a25f-179f7e283db9';

